//? Title: Unary coding: actual words and complete decoding
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Representing small nonnegative counts can use a delimiter instead of a length
field. Unary coding writes one mark per unit followed by zero; its simplicity
comes with linear length in the represented value.
)

\toc

> The method

The code for n is1 repeated n times, then0, giving length L(n)=n+1. The zero
delimiter makes concatenations uniquely decodable. For P(n)=2^(−n−1), Kraft sum
Σ2^(−L(n))=1 and −log2 P(n)=L(n); the mean length and entropy both equal2 bits.
This exact match is specific to that geometric source, not arbitrary integer
data.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/unary_coding_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/unary_coding.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto bits = a::unary_encode({0, 1, 3});
    auto decoded = a::unary_decode(bits, 3);
    std::print("| actual stream | actual decoded |\n|---|---|\n|`{}`|`{}`|\n",
               bits, decoded);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Counts0,1,3");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual emitted bits", bits.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual decoded {}", decoded));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/unary_coding_tiny.svg");
}
```
